  ],
  "notes": "Topic checks are regexes over the Name and QueryString of AWS::Logs::QueryDefinition (whole-resource path); the prompt describes topics only, so query bodies can't be pinned. Every template of this kind mentions tokens and users, so token and request checks need a rate form and a per-user grouping, and cost checks need a cost word and a grouping. Tiers: the three named groups (real-time, user and session, cost and attribution) are core; the 'additional debugging and analysis queries' are detail. 'about 19' is accepted as at least 15. 'organized into logical groups' and the review audience are not visible in a template and are unchecked. ua_session_usage can be satisfied by a token query grouped by session even if it is the cache one, since RE2 has no negative match. log_group_parameter is detail: the prompt describes the parameter (unnamed) as configuration surface, while the log-group value itself is core in all_scoped_to_log_group."
}
